= ChargePoint User Manual =

The '''ChargePoint''' program is a Python‑based [https://www.openchargealliance.org/ OCPP 1.6] charge point (EV charger) '''simulator'''. It emulates the behaviour of an electric‑vehicle charging station and communicates with an OCPP Central System (CSMS) over WebSocket. A web interface lets you simulate cable and car connections, start and stop charging sessions, view live energy data, and inspect the OCPP message log.

This manual describes how to '''install''', '''configure''', and '''use''' the ChargePoint simulator.

__TOC__

== Overview ==

The ChargePoint program is a '''pure software simulator''' — it does not interface with real charging hardware. Instead it:

* Simulates cable and car connection events from the web UI.
* Generates simulated power, per‑phase current, and accumulated energy.
* Connects to a CSMS over OCPP 1.6 and exchanges the standard messages.
* Responds to remote commands (RemoteStart/Stop, Reset, UnlockConnector, ChangeAvailability).
* Persists sessions, configuration, and OCPP logs to SQLite.

=== Architecture ===

<pre>
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│            ChargePoint Simulator             │
│                                              │
│  Flask + Socket.IO web GUI   ── SQLite DB    │
│  Port 5000 (default)                         │
│                                              │
│  OCPP 1.6 client (background asyncio thread) │
│        │                                     │
└────────┼─────────────────────────────────────┘
         ▼  ws://<csms>:9000/ocpp/<station_id>
   Central System (CSMS) — or via the OCPPProxy
</pre>

{| class="wikitable"
! Component !! File !! Responsibility
|-
| Entry point + web GUI || <code>chargepoint.py</code> || Flask + Socket.IO app, REST API, starts the OCPP thread
|-
| OCPP client / simulator || <code>cp_sim.py</code> || OCPP 1.6 message handling and energy simulation
|-
| Database layer || <code>db.py</code> || SQLite schema and data access
|-
| Data models || <code>models.py</code> || <code>Config</code>, <code>ChargeSession</code>, and <code>EmulatorState</code> dataclasses
|}

== Installation ==

=== Requirements ===

* '''Python 3.7+''' (uses async/await, type hints, f‑strings).
* Python packages (no <code>requirements.txt</code> is shipped; install these directly):

{| class="wikitable"
! Package !! Purpose
|-
| <code>flask</code> || Web GUI framework
|-
| <code>flask-socketio</code> || Real‑time UI updates
|-
| <code>ocpp</code> || OCPP 1.6 protocol implementation
|-
| <code>websockets</code> || WebSocket client to the CSMS
|}

<code>sqlite3</code> is part of the Python standard library.

=== Install steps ===

# Create the application, data, and log directories:
#: <pre>sudo mkdir -p /opt/charger/ChargePoint /opt/charger/data /var/log/charger</pre>
# Copy the ChargePoint source files into <code>/opt/charger/ChargePoint/</code>.
# Install dependencies (a virtual environment is recommended):
#: <pre>pip install flask flask-socketio ocpp websockets</pre>

=== Running manually ===

<pre>
# Use built-in defaults
python3 chargepoint.py

# Use a configuration file
python3 chargepoint.py --config /opt/charger/ChargePoint/config.json
</pre>

The only command‑line argument is <code>--config</code>, the path to a JSON configuration file. When omitted, built‑in defaults are used. The web GUI starts on the configured port (default '''5000'''); open <code>http://&lt;host&gt;:5000</code>.

=== Running as a systemd service ===

A service unit is provided (<code>systemd/charger-chargepoint.service</code>):

<pre>
[Unit]
Description=Charge Point Simulator
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
WorkingDirectory=/opt/charger/ChargePoint
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 /opt/charger/ChargePoint/chargepoint.py
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5

StandardOutput=file:/var/log/charger/chargepoint.stdout
StandardError=file:/var/log/charger/chargepoint.stderr

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
</pre>

To install and enable the service:

<pre>
sudo cp systemd/charger-chargepoint.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now charger-chargepoint
</pre>

{{Note|To run with a config file under systemd, append <code>--config /opt/charger/ChargePoint/config.json</code> to the <code>ExecStart</code> line.}}

